WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.340
- There is a special
technique that consultants use

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:05.720
to draft their slide presentations.

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:08.000
This is a technique that I've never seen

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.990
anybody use outside of consulting.

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:13.710
In this video I'm going to spill the tea

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:16.890
on a technique that I
used almost every day

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:19.660
when I was a project lead at McKinsey.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.550
And when I needed to
draft the presentations

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:24.883
that then I wanted the
whole team to work on.

00:00:24.883 --> 00:00:26.940
Welcome to another coffee break

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:29.410
here on my channel Firm Learning.

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:32.060
My name is Heinrich,
and here on my channel,

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:34.510
I want to help you become successful

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:36.840
in the first years of your career.

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:40.060
On this channel, I'm sharing
my tips and strategies

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:41.510
that I learned at McKinsey

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:45.290
and now working in a C-level
role at a German retailer.

00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:47.550
But now let's jump right into it.

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:51.480
How do consultants draft their presentations

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:55.070
and to give you a sneak peek
what the end product will be,

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:57.500
I will show you a slide presentation

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:01.420
that I recently drafted,
where I use this technique.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:03.300
So this is how it looks like guys,

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.160
so I'm holding this now in the camera,

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:07.640
I hope that you are able to see this.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:10.630
This is something that is
called a Mickey Mouse Master,

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:14.870
also strawman, it is a
draft of a presentation,

00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:16.730
that typically the project lead

00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:19.970
or the partner in a
consulting context creates.

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:22.820
I remember in one of the very first weeks

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:24.600
I was working at McKinsey,

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:28.150
the project lead of that study
asked me to sit with him,

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:30.210
he would just take a piece of paper

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:33.080
and he would create a
master just like that

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:34.320
of the presentation.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:36.300
Then he gave it to me and then this was

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:39.610
one of my very first tasks at McKinsey,

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:42.660
just to create a whole slide presentation,

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:46.080
just following exactly this technique.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:47.990
So how exactly does it work?

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:50.850
How do you create such
a Mickey Mouse Master

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:52.450
or such a strawman?

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:54.880
So in order to show you
now I have my computer

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:57.460
here in front of me, usually
you would rather do it

00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:00.800
on a piece of paper but
just for recording purpose,

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:02.210
this is a bit easier.

00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:05.700
And you will always start
by creating a basic grid

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:09.460
on your paper, just to
resembling the slides.

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:12.330
And now of course, the idea
is that each of these squares

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:15.740
resembles an individual page
later in the presentation.

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:17.880
So what you will always start with

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:21.760
is to come up with the
action title of the slides.

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:25.550
The action titles are very
special types of titles.

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:28.050
If you have no idea
what action titles are,

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:29.720
these are key concepts

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:32.170
when creating PowerPoint presentations,

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:34.570
and I will insert a link somewhere above

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:37.490
where I explain exactly
what an action title is

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:38.610
and how you set it up.

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:40.460
If you don't know what
it is really check it out

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:42.470
because it's super important to create

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:43.970
consulting style presentations.

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:46.130
So once you do that
number writing it here,

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:48.480
and let's now for instance,
just talk about a company

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:51.070
that wants to improve costs
or anything like that.

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:53.473
Then the first slide
could for instance say,

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:55.353
company

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:01.280
is in market

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:07.030
with x percent growth.

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:08.090
So just in the beginning,

00:03:08.090 --> 00:03:10.560
you maybe want to lay the
scene and just say okay,

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:13.430
actually the market
environment is doing quite well

00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:14.770
and the market is growing.

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:16.110
And what do we usually do is just to do

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:18.470
a brief version of the action title,

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:21.310
it doesn't need to be the
perfect version already,

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:23.740
just a brief sketch of
what the action title

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:24.990
is supposed to be in the end.

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:26.920
And then what you also do is just do

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:29.710
a basic sketch of the type of chart,

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:31.780
the type of graph that you want.

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:33.930
So here for instance,
you could do a bar chart

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:36.710
maybe with a CAGR inserted

00:03:36.710 --> 00:03:39.400
just to give you a gist
of what is going on.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.860
Then the next one could maybe
be that you want to highlight

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:44.840
that the company actually is
under competitive pressure.

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:48.950
So market share of company is
decreasing due to competition.

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:51.760
And here for instance, you could
do some relative bar charts

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:55.610
where they are all 100% just
to show how the market share

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:58.260
of a company changed over time.

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:01.030
So this is now the market
share you might want to depict.

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:02.520
Then this is now going down.

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:04.530
Next, maybe we want to
show how the profitability

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:08.330
of the company will be
affected in the long term.

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:10.940
So for instance, you could
now do a waterfall chart

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:13.620
from 2020 to 2021,

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:17.800
say profitability will go down by 200,000.

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:20.500
And then maybe next to
propose a couple of measures.

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:23.580
So for instance, there could
be three areas now, right,

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:26.360
where you believe that the
company needs to improve on

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:29.140
in order to survive and to make a shift

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:30.340
in this new environment.

00:04:30.340 --> 00:04:32.640
And the next maybe there
will be some backups

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:36.110
for these three parts one,
two, and three explaining

00:04:36.110 --> 00:04:38.800
how exactly these measures
are supposed to look like.

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:41.390
And then you can here
insert a couple of notes

00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:43.930
on what exactly is supposed
to be inserted here.

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:46.330
Next, maybe there's a
timeline for the project,

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:47.600
when will this be completed?

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:49.650
And then you write the project timeline

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:52.940
goes on to end of 2021.

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:54.820
This probably not the best action title,

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:56.750
but just something of this line,

00:04:56.750 --> 00:04:58.830
then you maybe draft a Gantt chart,

00:04:58.830 --> 00:05:00.790
if this is now, possibly to understand

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:03.430
how this might look like,
and so on, and so forth.

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:06.290
So I hope you get the
idea what I'm looking for.

00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:09.730
This is then how you will
draft the whole presentation.

00:05:09.730 --> 00:05:12.320
And then of course, this
is then a piece of paper

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:14.490
that you give on to your associate

00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:16.950
or if you're the partner, maybe
you then share it with a team

00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:18.060
or with a project lead,

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:20.970
asking them to create the
presentation like this,

00:05:20.970 --> 00:05:23.400
but you can also use it
the other way around.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:26.190
So if you are an associate
and you have an idea

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:30.000
of how to structure a document
that now you want to create,

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.480
now instead of really writing it all out,

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:34.830
instead of already
creating the whole document

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:36.420
and only then getting the feedback

00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:37.900
that maybe your project lead

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:40.310
actually wants to do it
the whole other way around.

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:43.380
What I always found is
super great way to do,

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:46.280
is just briefly sketching
your presentation

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:49.440
in such a way, sketching it in this way,

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:51.470
where you have then the whole document,

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:53.540
the whole presentation on paper,

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:56.610
you then go to your project
lead with this piece of paper

00:05:56.610 --> 00:05:58.510
and then you discuss the presentation,

00:05:58.510 --> 00:06:01.890
the whole flow of the
pages, the whole storyline.

00:06:01.890 --> 00:06:03.970
Just as you have it in your head

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:05.490
based on such a piece of paper.

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:07.850
And this will always lead to a very great

00:06:07.850 --> 00:06:10.980
and constructive discussion
with your team lead.

00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:13.710
And the best thing is
drafting something like this

00:06:13.710 --> 00:06:15.650
will only take you a couple of minutes,

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:17.780
so you haven't really
invested a lot of work.

00:06:17.780 --> 00:06:20.130
And if you find out that
your project lead

00:06:20.130 --> 00:06:22.040
would like to do it completely different,

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:24.780
would like to tell the story
in a completely different way,

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:28.420
you haven't already wasted
the time creating slides

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:30.800
that in the end will not even be used.

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:32.900
And this is something that unfortunately,

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:35.020
happens quite a lot in consulting

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:37.130
but I trust many corporate jobs as well.

